{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109102","id":2705567876,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6hQ7CE","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109102","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109102.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109102.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109102","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109102/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109102/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109102/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/11a13154debc168b9bbe9c6e8a72a51efaf305b1","number":109102,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GLTF: Fix minor niche edge case issues with accessors","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While working on refactoring this code, I figured I should make a separate PR for some immediate fixes. These should be cherry-picked to past branches.\r\n\r\n* Import: Change the normalized signed byte and signed short formulas to match the glTF specification which explicitly provides formulas that implementations must use.\r\n  * Impact: Almost none, files using normalized signed values are extremely rare as far as I know. But in any case, the old behavior would import with incorrect values.\r\n* Import: Fix incorrect pad skip bytes for 16-bit MAT3s while decoding. I fixed the encoding part in PR #108302 but for some reason I forgot to fix the decoding part at the same time.\r\n  * Impact: Practically none, the core glTF specification doesn't even use MAT3. But in any case, the old behavior would fail to import files if an extension contained such data.\r\n* Import: Add a comment about unpacking weights as floats being intentional even though glTF specifies VEC4.\r\n  * Impact: None, it's a comment.\r\n* Export: Fix indices incorrectly using 16-bit unsigned short when 65535, which is explicitly reserved by the glTF specification as a primitive restart value, so we must use 32-bit unsigned int instead in these cases.\r\n  * Impact: Rare, it's highly unlikely that an array of indices goes up to exactly 65535... but it's possible.\r\n* Export: Fix [`Mesh::ARRAY_WEIGHTS`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_mesh.html#enum-mesh-arraytype) being implicitly casted to `Array` when Godot's Mesh uses a PackedFloat32Array or PackedFloat64Array internally and we're reading floats from it, now it uses `PackedRealArray` (aka `Vector<real_t>`).\r\n  * Impact: No behavior difference, it's just faster performance. Variant can convert between PackedFloat32Array and PackedFloat64Array automatically just like it can convert between those two and Array, so now it performs either 0 or 1 conversions instead of always performing 1 conversion.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"h